276
00:10:57,980 --> 00:11:00,980
I'd rather call like Miyamura if you're just gonna tease me about the text.

277
00:11:00,980 --> 00:11:02,980
But Yanagi needs your text, Prez.

278
00:11:02,980 --> 00:11:03,980
Calls work too.

279
00:11:03,980 --> 00:11:06,980
The thought of you all calling that early when I don't do mornings.

280
00:11:06,980 --> 00:11:08,980
You have full permission to hang up without talking.

281
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:10,980
Waking you up is what matters.

282
00:11:10,980 --> 00:11:12,980
I apologize in advance.

283
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:14,980
What should a wake-up text say?

284
00:11:14,980 --> 00:11:15,980
Alright.

285
00:11:15,980 --> 00:11:17,980
I can't let them down.

286
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:45,980
What?

287
00:11:45,980 --> 00:11:46,980
It's morning.

288
00:11:46,980 --> 00:11:47,980
No way.

289
00:11:47,980 --> 00:11:48,980
It's only 1.30.

290
00:11:48,980 --> 00:11:49,980
That's night.

291
00:11:49,980 --> 00:11:51,980
I'm going back to sleep.

292
00:11:51,980 --> 00:11:52,980
Hey, Akane.

293
00:11:52,980 --> 00:11:53,980
This is your wake-up call.

294
00:11:53,980 --> 00:11:54,980
No, it's not.

295
00:11:54,980 --> 00:11:55,980
What?

296
00:11:55,980 --> 00:11:56,980
So tired.

297
00:11:56,980 --> 00:11:57,980
Hey, you answered.

298
00:11:57,980 --> 00:11:58,980
Good morning.

299
00:11:58,980 --> 00:11:59,980
Better get up, Rose.

300
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:00,980
I'm going back to sleep.

301
00:12:00,980 --> 00:12:02,980
I'm going back to sleep.

302
00:12:02,980 --> 00:12:05,980
I'm going back to sleep.

303
00:12:05,980 --> 00:12:06,980
Hey, Akane.

304
00:12:06,980 --> 00:12:07,980
This is your wake-up call.

305
00:12:07,980 --> 00:12:08,980
No, it's not.

306
00:12:08,980 --> 00:12:09,980
What?

307
00:12:09,980 --> 00:12:10,980
So tired.

308
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:11,980
Hey, Akane.

309
00:12:11,980 --> 00:12:12,980
This is your wake-up call.

310
00:12:12,980 --> 00:12:13,980
No, it's not.

311
00:12:13,980 --> 00:12:14,980
What?

312
00:12:14,980 --> 00:12:15,980
I'm tired.

313
00:12:15,980 --> 00:12:16,980
Hey, you answered.

314
00:12:16,980 --> 00:12:17,980
Good morning.

315
00:12:17,980 --> 00:12:18,980
Better get up, Rose.

316
00:12:18,980 --> 00:12:39,980
18-year-old Akane Yanagi is profoundly bad at getting out of bed.

317
00:12:39,980 --> 00:12:42,980
Oh, the text.

318
00:12:42,980 --> 00:12:45,980
Hey, I woke up in time.

319
00:12:45,980 --> 00:12:47,980
I really owe you one.

320
00:12:47,980 --> 00:12:50,980
I'm happy for you, but the way you hung up without a word definitely stopped.

321
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:51,980
I am so sorry.

322
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:53,980
I don't even remember since I was half asleep.

323
00:12:53,980 --> 00:12:54,980
Oh, there you are.

324
00:12:54,980 --> 00:12:57,980
Thank you for the text.

325
00:12:57,980 --> 00:12:58,980
I laughed until my sides hurt.

326
00:12:58,980 --> 00:12:59,980
You laughed?

327
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:00,980
Then I was up and at him.

328
00:13:00,980 --> 00:13:01,980
A good hearty laugh did the trick.

329
00:13:01,980 --> 00:13:03,980
So round two's a go for tomorrow?

330
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:05,980
No, but thank you.

331
00:13:05,980 --> 00:13:07,980
I should learn to be more independent, I think.

332
00:13:07,980 --> 00:13:09,980
Plus, I heard my alarm go off before anything.

333
00:13:09,980 --> 00:13:10,980
All right.

334
00:13:10,980 --> 00:13:12,980
But if you change your mind, just give me a shot.

335
00:13:12,980 --> 00:13:13,980
I will.

336
00:13:13,980 --> 00:13:18,980
Little did Yanagi know how much he'd regret this decision then.

337
00:13:18,980 --> 00:13:23,980
For his remaining alarm clock would also fall silent.

338
00:13:23,980 --> 00:13:24,980
You both yourself.

339
00:13:24,980 --> 00:13:34,980
Can't choose between oolong and green tea?

340
00:13:38,980 --> 00:13:39,980
Hey!

341
00:13:39,980 --> 00:13:40,980
Yanagi.

342
00:13:40,980 --> 00:13:45,460
No, it's fine. I simply needed a drink. As long as it quenches my thirst, it'll do.

343
00:13:45,740 --> 00:13:48,140
And this one happens to be brand new, I believe.

344
00:13:48,760 --> 00:13:54,580
I've noticed you're relaxed with your classmates and Yoshikawa, yet act so courteous with the rest of us.

345
00:13:54,940 --> 00:14:00,160
I suppose it's something of a habit. I'm a bit more casual when I speak with people I'm close to.

346
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:02,820
The same goes for people I want to be closer to.

347
00:14:02,820 --> 00:14:11,140
I worded that horribly, so please don't misinterpret what I said.

348
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:15,480
And it's not that I don't want to be friends with you or anyone else I'm more well-mannered around.

349
00:14:16,180 --> 00:14:17,940
The damage is done.

350
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:25,080
That's some aura. Wonder why Mr. Doom and Gloom is so down in the dumps.

351
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:26,000
What's the matter?

352
00:14:26,540 --> 00:14:29,140
Well, I'm all ears, pal. Give me them details.

353
00:14:29,140 --> 00:14:32,960
Go on and get it off of that chest. And shake till you feel better.

354
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:34,220
Up yours.

355
00:14:35,180 --> 00:14:35,780
Senkoku!

356
00:14:37,260 --> 00:14:39,220
Okay, that's on Shu for being a pest.

357
00:14:39,320 --> 00:14:40,560
I'm a lovable goofball!

358
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:42,460
Did you and your girl have an argument?

359
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:44,920
Rejection.

360
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:47,460
Shu, he says Ayasaki's single now.

361
00:14:47,820 --> 00:14:49,860
No, I did not! We're still dating!

362
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:52,980
So Yanagi rejected you.

363
00:14:53,500 --> 00:14:54,800
In here, I thought you were tight.

364
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:58,500
He said he's polite with me because he has zero intentions of getting any closer.

365
00:14:58,500 --> 00:15:00,080
That's why he's polite.

366
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:03,580
You want half of this chocolate Danish thing?

367
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:05,460
Sure. How kind.

368
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:07,080
I can't finish it on my own.

369
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:09,020
So it's a Danish?

370
00:15:09,520 --> 00:15:11,160
A really sweet Danish.

371
00:15:11,540 --> 00:15:13,000
All that chocolate gave me heartburn.

372
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:14,240
You like it?

373
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:14,880
Uh-huh.

374
00:15:15,680 --> 00:15:16,160
It's yummy.

375
00:15:18,380 --> 00:15:19,760
Oh, cool deal.

376
00:15:20,140 --> 00:15:21,740
Just, um, pace yourself, okay?

377
00:15:22,540 --> 00:15:23,040
Roger.

378
00:15:23,040 --> 00:15:28,380
Stop smirking like you beat me at something!

379
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:32,380
And you stop acting like you're the only one that he's overly formal with.

380
00:15:32,580 --> 00:15:34,360
What you said. It's no biggie.

381
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:36,080
I know, but still...

382
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:37,300
The Prez, Ayasaki.

383
00:15:37,960 --> 00:15:39,640
Everyone and their grandmother likes Yanagi.

384
00:15:40,640 --> 00:15:42,280
Okay, I won't let it bother me.

385
00:15:42,460 --> 00:15:44,580
I'll treat him the same way that I always have.

386
00:15:45,240 --> 00:15:47,680
Ah, stuck in the friend zone.

387
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:50,520
You know what it means to be out of the friend zone, right?

388
00:15:59,020 --> 00:15:59,580
Sengoku!

389
00:16:02,580 --> 00:16:03,100
Sorry!

390
00:16:03,720 --> 00:16:04,780
Please forgive me!

391
00:16:04,820 --> 00:16:07,780
I assure you it's okay, as long as it quenches my thirst.

392
00:16:07,780 --> 00:16:10,400
I don't think it did.

393
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:15,920
You know, if it tastes too strong, I wouldn't mind drinking it in your stead, so...

394
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:18,520
I'll snag you another drink real quick-like.

395
00:16:18,920 --> 00:16:19,960
It'll def-taste better.

396
00:16:20,180 --> 00:16:22,360
Thank you, but only if you really want to.

397
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:23,080
Totes!

398
00:16:28,160 --> 00:16:29,320
Here you...

399
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:30,520
I mean, trade ya.

400
00:16:30,920 --> 00:16:31,540
Cool deal?

401
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:33,540
Uh, yeah, that's great.

402
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:36,500
Lots of kids in my class don't like this juice.

403
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:39,180
I've heard its flavor can be best described as...

404
00:16:39,180 --> 00:16:39,660
Sucky.

405
00:16:40,140 --> 00:16:42,680
Uh, is he trying to be more casual with me?

406
00:16:44,460 --> 00:16:45,340
Hey, listen.

407
00:16:46,080 --> 00:16:47,880
Talk to me however you prefer.

408
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:50,660
Don't force yourself to use slang and stuff.

409
00:16:51,640 --> 00:16:53,360
But, I am...

410
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:53,660
Right!

411
00:16:54,100 --> 00:16:54,460
Yes!

412
00:16:54,780 --> 00:16:55,240
Ten-four!

413
00:16:59,240 --> 00:17:00,180
All right!

414
00:17:00,380 --> 00:17:01,460
Glad you understand.

415
00:17:01,460 --> 00:17:06,720
Sengoku's creeping me out.

416
00:17:07,140 --> 00:17:07,480
Oh?

417
00:17:07,580 --> 00:17:08,240
How come?

418
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:09,840
Because of that big dopey grin?

419
00:17:10,060 --> 00:17:10,680
Holy cow!

420
00:17:10,840 --> 00:17:11,980
That is really creepy.

421
00:17:13,040 --> 00:17:14,560
The creep slapped me!

422
00:17:14,960 --> 00:17:16,700
Sengoku's a pretty straightforward guy.

423
00:17:17,260 --> 00:17:18,420
He probably made up with Yanagi.

424
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:22,440
Yay!

425
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:24,060
Yanagi's here!

426
00:17:24,060 --> 00:17:25,900
Where's he heading to, though?

427
00:17:26,640 --> 00:17:28,100
I'm returning to the classroom.

428
00:17:28,260 --> 00:17:31,260
Remy won't let you take another step until you talk more casually.

429
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:33,640
Aw, don't laugh me off.

430
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:37,080
If only Sengoku were as blunt as Ayasaki when he spoke.

431
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:39,000
Yay!

432
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:40,020
Yanagi's here!

433
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:41,280
Where's he headed to, though?

434
00:17:41,640 --> 00:17:43,500
You're stuck near than a box of tissues.

435
00:17:43,980 --> 00:17:44,820
We're friends, aren't we?

436
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:45,640
Talk casually!

437
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:45,840
No.

438
00:17:47,640 --> 00:17:49,260
That would just be an imposter.

439
00:17:49,580 --> 00:17:51,040
You look like you're gonna cry.

440
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:52,060
What's wrong, huh?

441
00:17:52,060 --> 00:17:58,600
I could do not.

442
00:18:00,740 --> 00:18:01,180
Right.

443
00:18:01,580 --> 00:18:02,720
You ready for this, Iyuda?

444
00:18:03,740 --> 00:18:04,400
Yeah, yeah!

445
00:18:04,620 --> 00:18:05,600
Don't hold back!

446
00:18:05,700 --> 00:18:06,700
Because I sure won't.

447
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:08,100
Here I go.

448
00:18:09,060 --> 00:18:09,420
Ah-ha!

449
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:11,340
What the heck is this game?

450
00:18:11,660 --> 00:18:13,680
He said he could catch a blade with his hands.

451
00:18:14,020 --> 00:18:16,900
Since I thought it was a bold claim, I asked for a demonstration.

452
00:18:17,200 --> 00:18:18,080
Which he then failed.

453
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:21,760
Man, I so would have caught it if it had been a katana.

454
00:18:22,060 --> 00:18:24,180
He would make a murderer out of our sweet Yanagi.

455
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:27,480
Tell us you how nuts he is.

456
00:18:27,820 --> 00:18:28,400
I wonder.

457
00:18:29,360 --> 00:18:33,660
Suppose I took a page out of Iyuda's book and said I could catch a blade with my hands.

458
00:18:34,020 --> 00:18:36,560
Would Yanagi have asked me to demonstrate my skills, too?

459
00:18:37,280 --> 00:18:38,600
Um, hard to say.

460
00:18:39,220 --> 00:18:40,600
The people he's drawn to.

461
00:18:40,600 --> 00:18:46,540
They tend to possess rather cheerful demeanors, don't they?

462
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:48,400
You mean airheads like Yoshikawa?

463
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:50,080
If air-

464
00:18:50,080 --> 00:18:54,280
Cheerful people are easier for him to get along with, I don't stand a chance.

465
00:18:54,420 --> 00:18:56,340
Just embrace your inner airheadedness.

466
00:18:56,660 --> 00:18:58,640
When I saw Yoshikawa the other day...

467
00:18:58,640 --> 00:19:00,640
...and he's not even listening to me.

468
00:19:03,340 --> 00:19:04,440
Oh, where's she going?

469
00:19:06,260 --> 00:19:07,900
Oh, I'm so sorry!

470
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:10,700
She mistook the wall for a person and apologized?

471
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:12,240
Well, I've done that.

472
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:13,820
Oh, but wait, there's more.

473
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:20,480
Yes, she glared daggers at the wall she bumped into.

474
00:19:21,180 --> 00:19:23,520
I will never be anything like Yoshikawa.

475
00:19:23,740 --> 00:19:24,360
Neither.

476
00:19:25,280 --> 00:19:26,860
Okay, but how?

477
00:19:27,440 --> 00:19:30,580
Shu might be the type of person to imitate if you want to act friendlier, dude.

478
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:32,340
Imitating, Yura?

479
00:19:32,820 --> 00:19:35,060
I compromised far too much, so no!

480
00:19:35,300 --> 00:19:37,520
Better him than the girl who glares at walls.

481
00:19:38,360 --> 00:19:39,600
I'll show you how it's done, okay?

482
00:19:39,760 --> 00:19:40,620
Hang tight and watch.

483
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:41,360
Watching?

484
00:19:42,620 --> 00:19:43,060
Yanagi!

485
00:19:43,060 --> 00:19:44,160
That's me.

486
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:45,360
Tickle torture!

487
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:48,020
Akane's ticklish on the soles of his feet, too!

488
00:19:48,700 --> 00:19:49,460
Your turn.

489
00:19:49,900 --> 00:19:50,580
No way!

490
00:19:50,920 --> 00:19:52,220
Nope, not a chance!

491
00:19:52,340 --> 00:19:52,640
Never!

492
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:53,240
Idiot!

493
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:54,980
That kind of talk won't get you anywhere!

494
00:19:55,480 --> 00:19:56,980
You're better friends than you used to be!

495
00:19:57,240 --> 00:19:58,960
Now get over there and tickle that man!

496
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:02,060
All right, I have to practice before the real thing, though.

497
00:20:02,260 --> 00:20:04,820
You're seriously practicing for a tickle fight right now?

498
00:20:05,620 --> 00:20:06,060
There.

499
00:20:07,140 --> 00:20:09,520
I feel violated from how sensual that was!

500
00:20:09,920 --> 00:20:12,300
Yo, that took me by complete surprise!

501
00:20:12,300 --> 00:20:13,300
Keep it rated, Jade!

502
00:20:13,520 --> 00:20:16,260
I don't know what I did, or why you're angry with me.

503
00:20:16,880 --> 00:20:18,880
What you did is called a grope.

504
00:20:19,220 --> 00:20:20,480
Thank goodness I practiced.

505
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:22,260
Yanagi would have hated that.

506
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:24,500
So you're groping people now.

507
00:20:24,620 --> 00:20:26,980
Why do you pop in at the worst possible times?

508
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:28,820
Doing a bit of role play, are we?

509
00:20:28,960 --> 00:20:30,720
And Sengoku's playing the handsy pervert.

510
00:20:30,760 --> 00:20:31,220
Hey, now!

511
00:20:31,220 --> 00:20:32,780
What part are you playing, then?

512
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:33,840
Yanagi.

513
00:20:34,620 --> 00:20:36,460
Throw in the setting while you're at it!

514
00:20:36,600 --> 00:20:37,860
I'm gonna trade or something!

515
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:42,560
If the scene's Akane getting felt upon a train, who should I be?

516
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:47,000
Since it's a role you know inside and out, just be an airhead.

517
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:49,060
You really called somebody an airhead just now!

518
00:20:49,140 --> 00:20:51,320
Is the class president bullying me?

519
00:20:51,320 --> 00:20:52,580
No, calm down.

520
00:20:52,900 --> 00:20:53,740
He's just frustrated.

521
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:56,640
Wants to bridge a gap between a friend, but his missing parts.

522
00:20:56,880 --> 00:20:57,380
What gap?

523
00:20:57,600 --> 00:20:58,720
We're all peas in a pod.

524
00:20:58,880 --> 00:21:00,060
But he's unsatisfied?

525
00:21:00,580 --> 00:21:02,680
Am I the only one who thinks we're friends?

526
00:21:03,040 --> 00:21:05,420
This isn't about you and your life's not in danger!

527
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:06,260
So cut it out!

528
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:07,280
Aw, come on.

529
00:21:07,540 --> 00:21:08,740
Don't fight, guys.

530
00:21:08,880 --> 00:21:09,620
Really, people?

531
00:21:09,800 --> 00:21:10,500
Timing!

532
00:21:10,740 --> 00:21:12,460
The press is being mean to me.

533
00:21:12,640 --> 00:21:13,200
You're bullying?

534
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:14,520
Say it ain't so!

535
00:21:14,560 --> 00:21:15,720
You don't hate the hush!

536
00:21:15,720 --> 00:21:19,260
I really can't see Sengoku as a bully.

537
00:21:23,500 --> 00:21:26,320
You take his side like it's the one with the cream.

538
00:21:26,740 --> 00:21:28,100
Guess I never noticed.

539
00:21:28,660 --> 00:21:31,080
Sengoku and Yanagi sure are good friends.

540
00:21:32,220 --> 00:21:33,200
Discretion, please!

541
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:34,080
Guess what?

542
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:36,480
Sengoku told me he wants to be like Shu.

543
00:21:36,660 --> 00:21:37,120
He did?

544
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:38,020
But why?

545
00:21:38,800 --> 00:21:40,200
I like him just the way he is.

546
00:21:41,620 --> 00:21:42,660
What a surprise!

547
00:21:42,900 --> 00:21:44,040
To walk in Shu's shoes,

